course: dictionary
lesson: 3477
title: Fallow: resting land and quiet time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fallow has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one fits. When farmers leave a field fallow, they plough it but grow nothing on it for a season, so the soil can rest and get healthy again.
explain: Look at the clues. Words like crops, soil and seasons point to farming. A quiet period when nothing much is happening can also be fallow, so a «fallow period» is a slow time, not a field.
explain: Animal words work differently. In «red and fallow deer», the word deer tells you fallow is a kind of deer. Always ask what the word is doing in the sentence, then check your meaning by swapping it in.
fact: Fallow land is a field that is ploughed but left without crops for a season.
fact: Farmers let fields rest this way so the soil can get healthy again. This is part of crop rotation, where fields take turns to rest.
fact: «A fallow period» is a quiet time when not much is happening or being produced.
fact: A fallow deer is a smallish deer, light brown with white spots in summer.
fact: Six kinds of deer live wild in Britain, but only red and roe are native. People brought the other four, including fallow deer.
exercise: Farmers leave a field «fallow» for a season. Why? | So the crops grow twice as fast | So the field can be sold for houses | *So the soil can rest and get healthy again | So the tractors can be cleaned
exercise: «In autumn the stags roar and fight.» What is a fallow deer? | A quiet time with nothing happening | A huge bird that lives in fields | *A smallish deer, light brown with white spots in summer | A large black deer that lives in the Arctic
exercise: Mia says the school year has a «fallow period» in the summer. What does fallow mean in her sentence? | A time of heavy rain | A time when everyone is very busy | A time for planting seeds | *A quiet time when not much is happening
test: What does «lie fallow» mean? | To be ploughed deep and planted at once | To be sold to a builder | *To be left unplanted for a season so the soil can rest | To be covered in snow all winter
test: Which animal is a fallow deer? | A tiny brown bird | A deer that is native to Britain and always has been | *A smallish, light brown deer with white spots in summer | A large grey deer with huge antlers that lives by the sea
exam: In «Richmond Park has about 600 red and fallow deer», what clue shows that fallow is an animal? | The word about, which means nearby | The number 600, which is far too big | The word park before it | *The word deer after red and fallow
